index 4479b53..974b882 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,30 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Semantic components
+
+Components under `src/components/semantic/` do not take visual props. They take an article,
+derive a semantic context from it with `getSemanticContext` in `src/utils/semantics.ts`, and
+pick their treatment from the token maps in that file. The context has four axes:
+
+| Axis        | Derived from            | Drives                                                     |
+| ----------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
+| `desk`      | `category`              | accent colour, headline hover, section rule, hero overlay  |
+| `freshness` | `date` vs. a reference  | badge, dateline wording, headline weight, edge rule, tint  |
+| `depth`     | `readingTime`           | pips, headline scale, whether a summary or progress bar shows |
+| `tone`      | `tags` and the headline | kicker, headline typography, image aspect, byline          |
+
+Components:
+
+- `StoryCard` renders one story on a `lead`, `grid`, `row` or `compact` surface.
+- `SemanticSection` reads a list of stories, promotes a breaking one to the lead, takes on a shared
+  desk's colour, and chooses a layout from the count.
+- `DeskTag`, `FreshnessBadge`, `Dateline`, `ReadingDepth` are the atoms the card is built from.
+- `ReadingProgress` is a client component for article pages that renders nothing for quick reads,
+  a bar for standard reads, and a bar plus a minutes-left counter for long reads.
+
+Freshness is measured against a reference time. Sections default to the newest story they contain,
+so a static content corpus still exercises every state. Every rendered element carries
+`data-desk`, `data-freshness`, `data-depth` and `data-tone` attributes for styling hooks and for
+inspecting the derived context in DevTools. See `/semantics` for a living reference of all states.
